Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:07.480
The final data type we will cover for now is the&nbsp;
bool data type, short for Boolean. Boolean values&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:15.840
are either true or false or, in binary terms,&nbsp;
1 or 0. I have a code example, 114-boolean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:24.680
that shows a Boolean variable on line 1,&nbsp;
char_life, which is set to True. Part of learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:30.800
a programming language is learning the nuances&nbsp;
of its syntax. In most programming languages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:40.960
the words true and false represent Boolean values.&nbsp;
Notice that the True and False values on lines 1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:50.160
and 3 are title-cased, meaning they start with&nbsp;
capital letters. Python is case-sensitive in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:56.280
many spots, including this one. It is important&nbsp;
to learn these characteristics to use the correct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:04.320
casing for Boolean variables and avoid errors when&nbsp;
trying to run code containing them. To see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:10.720
results of this code, which returns a value based&nbsp;
on the status of a character's life for a game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:21.520
I will run the code, and the code works,&nbsp;
showing that I am still in the game. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:35.000
it fails if I change True to lowercase true and&nbsp;
try to rerun this code. We do see a message asking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:42.800
us if we meant to use the title-cased version&nbsp;
of the word, True, at least. To finish this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:50.440
unit on data types and operators, I will switch&nbsp;
to this file, 114-analyze, and here we have five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:58.040
print statements that display types for various&nbsp;
pieces of data. Go to your workbook and do the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:06.560
“Review 1.1” project to identify the data types&nbsp;
of each piece of data as a string, integer, float,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:14.280
or boolean. In the next video, we will reveal&nbsp;
and discuss the answers to the workbook project.

